### node://hrono/nodes/79/streamlink-cdp-tooling-parent-brief@43b0c3a2e6a3f3af57db557937777dd1aefdf70c9674bc397106a53e52e7aeff sp:/Streamlink%20CDP%20tooling%3A%20parent%20brief/Generated%20bindings%20%28do%20not%20edit%29/.list
- Every command is a generator that yields `{"method": "Domain.name", "params": {...}}` and receives the JSON response.
- The caller must send the yielded dict and feed the response back. The result is `StopIteration.value`.
- Snake_case Python names map to camelCase JSON keys. Keyword clashes get a trailing underscore (`id_`, `type_`, `hash_`, `format_`, `set_`, `dir_`, `filter_`).
- Optional params are included only when they are not `None`.
- Types are dataclasses or enums with `to_json`/`from_json`. Events are `@event_class("Domain.name")` dataclasses.
- Wrapper types subclass primitives: `Quad` (list), `ReportId` and `ScreenId` (str), `ExecutionContextId` (int).
- Many results are tuples such as `(RemoteObject, ExceptionDetails|None)`.

